#VRML V2.0 utf8
# Alps EC11E stand-in. KiCad ships no 3D models for the Rotary_Encoder library,
# and these three parts are what fills the 6.5 mm between the front board and the
# panel, so a 3D view without them answers nothing.
#
# Footprint outline and shaft axis are taken from the KiCad footprint itself
# (F.Fab box, MP lug positions): body 12.0 x 11.6, axis at 7.5 / 2.5.
# The heights are EC11E nominal: body 6.4, M7 bushing 5.0, shaft to 20 mm above
# the board. An approximation for clearance checks, not a datasheet model.
#
# VRML units are 0.1 inch, which is why every number here is millimetres / 2.54.
# Cylinders are written out as 24-sided prisms because KiCad's VRML reader
# ignores the Cylinder node.
Transform { children [

  # body
  Transform { translation 2.95276 -0.98425 1.25984
    children Shape {
      appearance Appearance { material Material { diffuseColor 0.08 0.08 0.09 specularColor 0.15 0.15 0.15 shininess 0.2 } }
      geometry Box { size 4.72441 4.56693 2.51969 }
    }
  }

  # M7 bushing
